# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (Vite). Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
#
# WARNING: every VITE_* variable is inlined into the public JavaScript bundle
# at build time. Only put values here that are safe for anyone to read. Secrets
# belong in Edge Function secrets — see the bottom of this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project URL and anon (publishable) key.
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API. The anon key is public by design; access
# is controlled by the RLS policies in supabase/migrations/.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-key"

# Set to "true" only once a Stripe account exists AND the
# create-checkout-session Edge Function is deployed. While unset, the donation
# section shows a "coming soon" notice with a contact address instead of a
# button that can only fail.
# VITE_DONATIONS_ENABLED="true"

# Set to "true" only once all three of these hold. While unset, the RSVP
# confirmation screen does not claim an email was sent.
#
#   1. RESEND_API_KEY is set in the Edge Function secrets.
#   2. The trigger on `rsvps` that calls send-rsvp-confirmation exists. It is
#      created by a migration, not by hand in the dashboard — the dashboard's
#      own "Database Webhooks" builder needs a schema that only appears once
#      the feature has been switched on in the UI there.
#   3. A sending domain is verified in Resend. This is the one that is easy to
#      miss: without it Resend falls back to its shared onboarding sender and
#      delivers **only to the Resend account owner's address**. Mail to the
#      owner arrives, everything looks healthy, and every actual visitor gets
#      nothing while the site tells them to check their inbox.
#
# VITE_EMAIL_ENABLED="true"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Actions
#
# The two variables above must also exist as repository secrets
# (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions) or the production build will
# ship with an unconfigured backend. See .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edge Function secrets — NEVER prefix these with VITE_ and never commit real
# values. Set them with:
#
#   npx supabase secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_... RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY       Stripe secret key (sk_test_… / sk_live_…)
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET   Signing secret for the stripe-webhook endpoint
#                           (whsec_…). Without it the webhook rejects
#                           everything, which is the correct default.
#   RESEND_API_KEY          Resend API key for transactional email
#   MAIL_FROM               Verified sender, e.g. "PAWTX <info@pawtx.org>"
#   CONTACT_INBOX           Where contact-form mail is delivered
#                           (default: paowtx@gmail.com)
#   SITE_URL                Allowed origins for Stripe return URLs, comma
#                           separated; the first is the default. Include the
#                           GitHub Pages project path. e.g.
#                           https://<user>.github.io/peace-academy-of-west-texas,http://localhost:3000
#                           A request may only return to one of these origins.
#   ORG_EIN                 The organization's real EIN. Donation receipts omit
#                           the tax ID line entirely until this is set — a
#                           placeholder EIN on a receipt would be a forged
#                           tax document.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Gemini AI social-feed summary.
#
# Setting this at build time publishes the key in the bundle. Prefer moving the
# summary call into an Edge Function before using a paid key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_KEY=""
